Z||000004||Archie||05-07-2001||08:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><BR>One of Ed's "partners" said that the 88 cradle is weaker than than the earlier years. Needs to be reinforced to withstand the torque of anything larger than a 3.4.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Whoever said that is wrong.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||05-07-2001||09:18 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> Whoever said that is wrong.<P>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Okay. What this guy said, exactly, was that he had seen a 3.8 conversion in an 88 that had bent/damaged the cradle, to the point where the owner called the fabricator (not Ed) and said "come pick it up!" <BR>I interpreted this as "anything larger than a 3.4..." <P>So, is the 88 cradle as sturdy as the earlier years?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Archie||05-07-2001||09:39 PM||||Well the guy is talking out of his hat or there is some other factor that contributed to the cradle bending, like an accident.<P>Actually, I think the guy is pulling your leg to see how tall of a story you'll bite down on.<P>I'll bet I have 200 customers who have use the '88 for their V-8 swaps & I've never heard of cradles bending.<P>Archie||||reg||1
